{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019YKAgLLYtiAC447fTtb49T","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Central store of GM vocabulary and answer conventions CONFIRMED by correct submissions.\n\nAdd to this whenever the Game Master accepts/rejects a specific spelling, so future solvers emit the\nexact wording the GM wants instead of re-hitting the wrong-answer cap. Each entry notes where it was proven.\n\"\"\"\n\n# ELF header fields (binary-reverse-engineering), confirmed Day 1 \"ELF Aware\".\nELF_ENDIANNESS = {\"ELFDATA2LSB\": \"little\", \"ELFDATA2MSB\": \"big\"}        # GM rejected \"little endian\"\nELF_MACHINE = {\"EM_X86_64\": \"x86-64\", \"EM_386\": \"x86\", \"EM_AARCH64\": \"AArch64\", \"EM_ARM\": \"ARM\"}  # not \"EM_X86_64\"\nELF_CLASS = {\"ELFCLASS32\": \"ELF32\", \"ELFCLASS64\": \"ELF64\"}             # readelf style, not \"ELFCLASS64\"\n# Day 8 \"Swift Justice\": answer_format.kind \"integer\" on the SAME field names -> elf_class = bit width \"64\" (not EI_CLASS\n# byte 2), machine = decimal e_machine \"62\" (single + TT + Mastery, 0 wrong; d01 text ELF64/x86-64 accepted alongside).\nELF_CLASS_BITS = {\"ELFCLASS32\": \"32\", \"ELFCLASS64\": \"64\"}\nELF_TYPE_AS_IS = True   # e_type submitted as the constant, e.g. \"ET_EXEC\" (not \"EXEC\")\n# Binary container \"format\" field (Day 2 \"Mangled\" cpp_format): bare lowercase family name.\n# CONFIRMED PER-FIELD (single-field submits, 2026-10-04): ELF -> \"elf\", PE -> \"pe\".\n# The earlier \"every PE spelling rejected\" lore was a MEASUREMENT ARTIFACT: a per-SET POST is all-or-nothing, so\n# \"pe\" always looked rejected only because the SAME PE set also had wrong mangled_score_symbol / vtable_symbol\n# (the GM wants their COFF COMDAT section-name form '.text$<sym>' / '.rdata$<sym>' for PE, not the bare symbol).\n# Once those two are fixed, \"pe\" is accepted and the PE set completes. Rejected ELF spellings: ELF, ELF64,\n# elf64-x86-64, HCFG, json.\nBINARY_FORMAT = {\"ELF\": \"elf\", \"PE\": \"pe\", \"MACHO\": \"macho\"}\n\n\ndef binary_format(kind, member_name=\"\", pe_magic=None):\n    \"\"\"GM `*_format` answer for a parsed container kind (\"ELF\"/\"PE\"/...); pe_magic = OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic.\"\"\"\n    return BINARY_FORMAT.get(kind, kind.lower())\n\n# Day 3 \"Table Manners\" (binary, managed-configuration), confirmed per-field 2026-10-04:\nPE_MACHINE = {0x14c: \"i386\", 0x8664: \"x86-64\", 0xaa64: \"AArch64\", 0x1c0: \"ARM\"}  # PE FILE_HEADER.Machine; \"x86\" REJECTED for a PE32 i386 .NET assembly; x86-64 GM-confirmed on c_machine/slot*_machine (the lib copy lacked it -> from-scratch replay emitted \"0x8664\" and failed binary TT twice)\n# ELF `section_names`: pyelftools [s.name for s in iter_sections()] INCLUDING the \"\" NULL section (without it: rejected).\n# ELF `symbols`: [s.name for s in .symtab if s.name] in table order, dupes kept (with the \"\" entries: rejected).\n# .NET `metadata_version`: CLI metadata root (BSJB) version string, e.g. \"v4.0.30319\".\n# ELF `disassembly` CONFIRMED 2026-10-04 (Table Manners single): the recover_code leaf rendered as capstone intel\n# \"{mnemonic} {op_str}\" with the DEFAULT ', ' separator but immediates in DECIMAL, e.g. [\"mov eax, 8100\",\"ret\"]\n# (8100 == 0x1fa4). Hex immediates / no-space-after-comma / \"ret \" / main / whole .text / _start..hlt all REJECTED.\n# .NET assembly `format` CONFIRMED 2026-10-04 (GM accepted): \"pe_cli\" — a PE container holding CLI (Common Language\n# Infrastructure / ECMA-335) metadata. The compound names the container + managed runtime, parallel to elf/pe for\n# native binaries. Methodology lesson: the generator composes real-spec terms (pe + cli), it does NOT use the common\n# analyst synonyms (msil/cil/dotnet/.net/managed were ALL wrong). Same discipline cracked batch control = if_guard.\nDOTNET_FORMAT = \"pe_cli\"\n# Day 4 \"Go Fish\" (Go ELF, go1.25 buildinfo GOARCH=amd64): `architecture` CONFIRMED \"x86-64\" = the ELF machine\n# vocabulary (ELF_MACHINE above), NOT the Go GOARCH token (\"amd64\" REJECTED). Go config was the same HCFG blob.\nARCHITECTURE_USES_MACHINE_VOCAB = True\nARCHITECTURE_REJECTED = [\"amd64\"]\n# Day 6 \"Pool Party\" (binary, java-bytecode-loader), confirmed 2026-10-06: a Java .jar's `format` is plain \"jar\"\n# (the archive/container name, like elf/pe). The container_runtime compound \"jar_jvm\" was REJECTED, so the pe_cli\n# law does NOT extend to Java. The HCFG config sat base64'd in a constant-pool String (static final CONFIG).\n# Day 7 \"Routine Check\" re-confirmed \"jar\" for a Kotlin fat jar (single 22f8c079, TT, Mastery; 0 wrong): the JVM\n# source language does not change the container label. HCFG `hcfg_version` = the blob's version as plain decimal (\"1\",\n# D6+D7 confirmed).\n# Day 9 \"Nimble\" (Nim ELF; single + TT + Mastery 5 sets, 0 wrong): NEW field `hcfg_offset` = plain decimal FILE offset of\n# the stored blob's first byte -- for a base64 Nim string literal, where the base64 TEXT starts (\"30696\" = 0x77e8: after\n# the 8-byte cap/flag word at 0x77e0, NOT that header and NOT the VA 0x4077e8). Raw/hex-blob offsets still unconfirmed.\n# Day 11 \"D-Day\" (D-language static ELF x86-64; single + TT + Mastery 3 sets, 0 wrong) re-confirmed the same law: the\n# base64 'SENGRw...' text sits NUL-terminated in .rodata right after a \".debug_line\\0\" string; hcfg_offset = \"368272\"\n# (0x59e90) = first byte of the base64 TEXT, same in all 3 D builds (sha differed, offset did not).\n# Day 12 \"Pascal's Wager\" (Free Pascal static ELF x86-64 inside a d01..d12 archive; single + TT + Mastery 3 sets) CONFIRMED\n# the RAW form: the blob sits un-encoded ('HCFG' magic + version/crc header + XOR'd body) and hcfg_offset = file offset of\n# the 'H' of the magic (\"82928\" = 0x143f0, all sets). The solver's raw-scan path returned \"none\" -> 1 lost submit.\nPLAYBOOK = [\n    # ---- binary-reverse-engineering --------------------------------------------------------------\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"format\",),\n        rule=\"Lowercase family name. NATIVE binary = the container only (elf/pe/macho). MANAGED binary = a \"\n             \"container+runtime COMPOUND naming the real-spec terms (a .NET PE is `pe_cli`: PE container + CLI/\"\n             \"ECMA-335 runtime), NOT an analyst synonym.\",\n        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.BINARY_FORMAT.values()) | {K.DOTNET_FORMAT})),\n        rejected=tuple(K.DOTNET_FORMAT_REJECTED) + (\"ELF\", \"ELF64\", \"elf64-x86-64\", \"PE32\", \"PE32+\"),\n        examples=(\"ELF->elf\", \"native PE->pe\", \".NET PE->pe_cli (pe+cli)\"),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"symbol\",),\n        rule=\"ELF: the BARE Itanium mangled name (_ZNK.., _ZTV..). PE/COFF (MinGW): the COMDAT SECTION-NAME form \"\n             \"— functions `.text$<mangled>`, vtables/typeinfo `.rdata$<mangled>`. Pick by the container, not the OS.\",\n        examples=(\"ELF vtable->_ZTV..\", \"PE function->.text$_ZN..\", \"PE vtable->.rdata$_ZTV..\"),\n        derive=_symbol_derive,\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"disassembly\",),\n        rule=\"Capstone INTEL syntax, `\\\"{mnemonic} {op_str}\\\"` with the default ', ' operand separator, but render \"\n             \"IMMEDIATES IN DECIMAL (e.g. 'mov eax, 8100', not 0x1fa4). One string per instruction.\",\n        examples=(\"mov eax,0x1fa4 -> 'mov eax, 8100'\",),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"endianness\",),\n        rule=\"Bare word: 'little' / 'big' (NOT 'little endian').\",\n        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.ELF_ENDIANNESS.values()))), rejected=(\"little endian\", \"big endian\", \"lsb\", \"msb\"),\n        closed=True,\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"machine\",),\n        rule=\"ELF e_machine -> x86-64 / x86 / AArch64 / ARM (not the EM_* constant). PE FILE_HEADER.Machine 0x14c \"\n             \"-> 'i386' (NOT 'x86' for a PE). answer_format.kind integer (D8): the decimal e_machine, e.g. 62.\",\n        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.ELF_MACHINE.values()) | set(K.PE_MACHINE.values()) | {\"62\"})),\n        rejected=(\"EM_X86_64\", \"x86_64\", \"amd64\"), examples=(\"PE32 i386 .NET -> i386\",),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"class\",),\n        rule=\"readelf style: 'ELF32' / 'ELF64' (not the ELFCLASS* constant). answer_format.kind integer (D8): the bit \"\n             \"width '32' / '64' -- NOT the raw EI_CLASS byte 1 / 2.\",\n        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.ELF_CLASS.values()) | {\"32\", \"64\"})), rejected=(\"ELFCLASS64\", \"ELFCLASS32\", \"1\", \"2\"),\n        closed=True,\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"type\",),\n24:BINARY = \"binary-reverse-engineering\"\n88:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"format\",),\n92:        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.BINARY_FORMAT.values()) | {K.DOTNET_FORMAT})),\n97:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"symbol\",),\n104:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"disassembly\",),\n110:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"endianness\",),\n116:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"machine\",),\n123:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"class\",),\n130:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"type\",),\n135:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"architecture\",),\n143:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"names\",),\n148:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"symbols\",),\n153:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"version\",),\n159:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"offset\",),","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abe32548-ece9-42ab-bb0b-c487167ec2d9","uuid":"5d01a1f0-6382-4e93-94d5-5227eb5fd41a","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:08:48.181Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Central store of GM vocabulary and answer conventions CONFIRMED by correct submissions.\n\nAdd to this whenever the Game Master accepts/rejects a specific spelling, so future solvers emit the\nexact wording the GM wants instead of re-hitting the wrong-answer cap. Each entry notes where it was proven.\n\"\"\"\n\n# ELF header fields (binary-reverse-engineering), confirmed Day 1 \"ELF Aware\".\nELF_ENDIANNESS = {\"ELFDATA2LSB\": \"little\", \"ELFDATA2MSB\": \"big\"}        # GM rejected \"little endian\"\nELF_MACHINE = {\"EM_X86_64\": \"x86-64\", \"EM_386\": \"x86\", \"EM_AARCH64\": \"AArch64\", \"EM_ARM\": \"ARM\"}  # not \"EM_X86_64\"\nELF_CLASS = {\"ELFCLASS32\": \"ELF32\", \"ELFCLASS64\": \"ELF64\"}             # readelf style, not \"ELFCLASS64\"\n# Day 8 \"Swift Justice\": answer_format.kind \"integer\" on the SAME field names -> elf_class = bit width \"64\" (not EI_CLASS\n# byte 2), machine = decimal e_machine \"62\" (single + TT + Mastery, 0 wrong; d01 text ELF64/x86-64 accepted alongside).\nELF_CLASS_BITS = {\"ELFCLASS32\": \"32\", \"ELFCLASS64\": \"64\"}\nELF_TYPE_AS_IS = True   # e_type submitted as the constant, e.g. \"ET_EXEC\" (not \"EXEC\")\n# Binary container \"format\" field (Day 2 \"Mangled\" cpp_format): bare lowercase family name.\n# CONFIRMED PER-FIELD (single-field submits, 2026-10-04): ELF -> \"elf\", PE -> \"pe\".\n# The earlier \"every PE spelling rejected\" lore was a MEASUREMENT ARTIFACT: a per-SET POST is all-or-nothing, so\n# \"pe\" always looked rejected only because the SAME PE set also had wrong mangled_score_symbol / vtable_symbol\n# (the GM wants their COFF COMDAT section-name form '.text$<sym>' / '.rdata$<sym>' for PE, not the bare symbol).\n# Once those two are fixed, \"pe\" is accepted and the PE set completes. Rejected ELF spellings: ELF, ELF64,\n# elf64-x86-64, HCFG, json.\nBINARY_FORMAT = {\"ELF\": \"elf\", \"PE\": \"pe\", \"MACHO\": \"macho\"}\n\n\ndef binary_format(kind, member_name=\"\", pe_magic=None):\n    \"\"\"GM `*_format` answer for a parsed container kind (\"ELF\"/\"PE\"/...); pe_magic = OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic.\"\"\"\n    return BINARY_FORMAT.get(kind, kind.lower())\n\n# Day 3 \"Table Manners\" (binary, managed-configuration), confirmed per-field 2026-10-04:\nPE_MACHINE = {0x14c: \"i386\", 0x8664: \"x86-64\", 0xaa64: \"AArch64\", 0x1c0: \"ARM\"}  # PE FILE_HEADER.Machine; \"x86\" REJECTED for a PE32 i386 .NET assembly; x86-64 GM-confirmed on c_machine/slot*_machine (the lib copy lacked it -> from-scratch replay emitted \"0x8664\" and failed binary TT twice)\n# ELF `section_names`: pyelftools [s.name for s in iter_sections()] INCLUDING the \"\" NULL section (without it: rejected).\n# ELF `symbols`: [s.name for s in .symtab if s.name] in table order, dupes kept (with the \"\" entries: rejected).\n# .NET `metadata_version`: CLI metadata root (BSJB) version string, e.g. \"v4.0.30319\".\n# ELF `disassembly` CONFIRMED 2026-10-04 (Table Manners single): the recover_code leaf rendered as capstone intel\n# \"{mnemonic} {op_str}\" with the DEFAULT ', ' separator but immediates in DECIMAL, e.g. [\"mov eax, 8100\",\"ret\"]\n# (8100 == 0x1fa4). Hex immediates / no-space-after-comma / \"ret \" / main / whole .text / _start..hlt all REJECTED.\n# .NET assembly `format` CONFIRMED 2026-10-04 (GM accepted): \"pe_cli\" — a PE container holding CLI (Common Language\n# Infrastructure / ECMA-335) metadata. The compound names the container + managed runtime, parallel to elf/pe for\n# native binaries. Methodology lesson: the generator composes real-spec terms (pe + cli), it does NOT use the common\n# analyst synonyms (msil/cil/dotnet/.net/managed were ALL wrong). Same discipline cracked batch control = if_guard.\nDOTNET_FORMAT = \"pe_cli\"\n# Day 4 \"Go Fish\" (Go ELF, go1.25 buildinfo GOARCH=amd64): `architecture` CONFIRMED \"x86-64\" = the ELF machine\n# vocabulary (ELF_MACHINE above), NOT the Go GOARCH token (\"amd64\" REJECTED). Go config was the same HCFG blob.\nARCHITECTURE_USES_MACHINE_VOCAB = True\nARCHITECTURE_REJECTED = [\"amd64\"]\n# Day 6 \"Pool Party\" (binary, java-bytecode-loader), confirmed 2026-10-06: a Java .jar's `format` is plain \"jar\"\n# (the archive/container name, like elf/pe). The container_runtime compound \"jar_jvm\" was REJECTED, so the pe_cli\n# law does NOT extend to Java. The HCFG config sat base64'd in a constant-pool String (static final CONFIG).\n# Day 7 \"Routine Check\" re-confirmed \"jar\" for a Kotlin fat jar (single 22f8c079, TT, Mastery; 0 wrong): the JVM\n# source language does not change the container label. HCFG `hcfg_version` = the blob's version as plain decimal (\"1\",\n# D6+D7 confirmed).\n# Day 9 \"Nimble\" (Nim ELF; single + TT + Mastery 5 sets, 0 wrong): NEW field `hcfg_offset` = plain decimal FILE offset of\n# the stored blob's first byte -- for a base64 Nim string literal, where the base64 TEXT starts (\"30696\" = 0x77e8: after\n# the 8-byte cap/flag word at 0x77e0, NOT that header and NOT the VA 0x4077e8). Raw/hex-blob offsets still unconfirmed.\n# Day 11 \"D-Day\" (D-language static ELF x86-64; single + TT + Mastery 3 sets, 0 wrong) re-confirmed the same law: the\n# base64 'SENGRw...' text sits NUL-terminated in .rodata right after a \".debug_line\\0\" string; hcfg_offset = \"368272\"\n# (0x59e90) = first byte of the base64 TEXT, same in all 3 D builds (sha differed, offset did not).\n# Day 12 \"Pascal's Wager\" (Free Pascal static ELF x86-64 inside a d01..d12 archive; single + TT + Mastery 3 sets) CONFIRMED\n# the RAW form: the blob sits un-encoded ('HCFG' magic + version/crc header + XOR'd body) and hcfg_offset = file offset of\n# the 'H' of the magic (\"82928\" = 0x143f0, all sets). The solver's raw-scan path returned \"none\" -> 1 lost submit.\nPLAYBOOK = [\n    # ---- binary-reverse-engineering --------------------------------------------------------------\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"format\",),\n        rule=\"Lowercase family name. NATIVE binary = the container only (elf/pe/macho). MANAGED binary = a \"\n             \"container+runtime COMPOUND naming the real-spec terms (a .NET PE is `pe_cli`: PE container + CLI/\"\n             \"ECMA-335 runtime), NOT an analyst synonym.\",\n        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.BINARY_FORMAT.values()) | {K.DOTNET_FORMAT})),\n        rejected=tuple(K.DOTNET_FORMAT_REJECTED) + (\"ELF\", \"ELF64\", \"elf64-x86-64\", \"PE32\", \"PE32+\"),\n        examples=(\"ELF->elf\", \"native PE->pe\", \".NET PE->pe_cli (pe+cli)\"),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"symbol\",),\n        rule=\"ELF: the BARE Itanium mangled name (_ZNK.., _ZTV..). PE/COFF (MinGW): the COMDAT SECTION-NAME form \"\n             \"— functions `.text$<mangled>`, vtables/typeinfo `.rdata$<mangled>`. Pick by the container, not the OS.\",\n        examples=(\"ELF vtable->_ZTV..\", \"PE function->.text$_ZN..\", \"PE vtable->.rdata$_ZTV..\"),\n        derive=_symbol_derive,\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"disassembly\",),\n        rule=\"Capstone INTEL syntax, `\\\"{mnemonic} {op_str}\\\"` with the default ', ' operand separator, but render \"\n             \"IMMEDIATES IN DECIMAL (e.g. 'mov eax, 8100', not 0x1fa4). One string per instruction.\",\n        examples=(\"mov eax,0x1fa4 -> 'mov eax, 8100'\",),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"endianness\",),\n        rule=\"Bare word: 'little' / 'big' (NOT 'little endian').\",\n        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.ELF_ENDIANNESS.values()))), rejected=(\"little endian\", \"big endian\", \"lsb\", \"msb\"),\n        closed=True,\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"machine\",),\n        rule=\"ELF e_machine -> x86-64 / x86 / AArch64 / ARM (not the EM_* constant). PE FILE_HEADER.Machine 0x14c \"\n             \"-> 'i386' (NOT 'x86' for a PE). answer_format.kind integer (D8): the decimal e_machine, e.g. 62.\",\n        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.ELF_MACHINE.values()) | set(K.PE_MACHINE.values()) | {\"62\"})),\n        rejected=(\"EM_X86_64\", \"x86_64\", \"amd64\"), examples=(\"PE32 i386 .NET -> i386\",),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"class\",),\n        rule=\"readelf style: 'ELF32' / 'ELF64' (not the ELFCLASS* constant). answer_format.kind integer (D8): the bit \"\n             \"width '32' / '64' -- NOT the raw EI_CLASS byte 1 / 2.\",\n        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.ELF_CLASS.values()) | {\"32\", \"64\"})), rejected=(\"ELFCLASS64\", \"ELFCLASS32\", \"1\", \"2\"),\n        closed=True,\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"type\",),\n24:BINARY = \"binary-reverse-engineering\"\n88:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"format\",),\n92:        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.BINARY_FORMAT.values()) | {K.DOTNET_FORMAT})),\n97:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"symbol\",),\n104:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"disassembly\",),\n110:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"endianness\",),\n116:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"machine\",),\n123:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"class\",),\n130:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"type\",),\n135:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"architecture\",),\n143:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"names\",),\n148:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"symbols\",),\n153:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"version\",),\n159:        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"offset\",),","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019YKAgLLYtiAC447fTtb49T","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8BH2fgucSfw5VuyFHjn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BbNNvXv6i6Ncdgc7Am4Mt5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; sed -n 1,48p lib/playbook.py; sed -n 130,200p lib/playbook.py; sed -n 60,110p lib/knowledge.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4708,"cache_read_input_tokens":42016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4708},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abe32548-ece9-42ab-bb0b-c487167ec2d9","uuid":"ba47f3f2-c785-4298-ab81-18e8e8907670","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:08:50.360Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8BH2KMngxbQwfNeHfhu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BbNNvXv6i6Ncdgc7Am4Mt5":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; sed -n 1,48p lib/playbook.py; sed -n 130,200p lib/playbook.py; sed -n 60,110p lib/knowledge.py"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BbNNvXv6i6Ncdgc7Am4Mt5","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Per-lane field playbooks: the GM's label GRAMMAR per field family.\n\nThe dominant failure on the binary and script lanes is not analysis, it is spelling the GM's synthetic\nlabel (e.g. `pe_cli`, `if_guard`, `.text$<sym>`) under coarse per-set feedback. `lib/knowledge.py` holds the\nconfirmed VALUES and `lib/vocab.json` the confirmed label lists; this module adds, per (lane, field-family):\nthe derivation RULE, the known-REJECTED spellings, and worked examples, and exposes them to the two consumers\nthat need them up front:\n\n  - for_lane(lane)                         -> markdown block injected into the worker prompts (point: start\n                                              from the rule, not blind synonyms)\n  - entry_for(lane, aid)                   -> the PlaybookEntry matching a field by its ending, or None\n  - rejected(lane, aid)                    -> spellings already proven wrong for this family (never reprobe)\n  - seed_candidates(lane, aid, terms, v)   -> high-priority label candidates for `hctf labels`, built from the\n                                              rule (closed vocab, or container+runtime / keyword+ending compounds)\n\nSingle source of truth for the confirmed values stays in lib/knowledge.py (imported below). Add a new family\nhere the moment the GM confirms one, next to the knowledge.py entry.\n\"\"\"\nimport re\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\nfrom . import knowledge as K\n\nBINARY = \"binary-reverse-engineering\"\nSCRIPT = \"script-analysis\"\nMETADATA = \"metadata-forensics\"\n\n\ndef field_family(aid):\n    \"\"\"Group fields by their trailing token: 'batch-launcher-control'->'control', 'd03_analysis_format'->'format',\n    'set2.cpp-mangled_score_symbol'->'symbol'. Mirrors hctf.labels.ending so the resolver and playbook agree.\"\"\"\n    last = str(aid).rsplit(\".\", 1)[-1]\n    parts = [p for p in re.split(r\"[-_]\", last) if p]\n    return parts[-1].lower() if parts else last.lower()\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass PlaybookEntry:\n    lanes: tuple           # lanes this applies to\n    families: tuple        # field-family endings (field_family(aid)) it covers\n    rule: str              # the derivation rule, one or two sentences\n    confirmed: tuple = ()  # GM-accepted values seen so far (closed vocab = the whole set)\n    rejected: tuple = ()   # GM-rejected spellings: never reprobe these\n    examples: tuple = ()   # worked (artifact-feature -> label) notes\n    closed: bool = False   # True: confirmed is the COMPLETE allowed set (probe only these)\n    derive: object = None  # optional fn(terms, solver_value) -> [candidate, ...] for compound labels\n\n\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"type\",),\n        rule=\"e_type submitted AS THE CONSTANT, e.g. 'ET_EXEC', 'ET_DYN' (not 'EXEC').\",\n        examples=(\"ET_EXEC\", \"ET_DYN\"),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"architecture\",),\n        rule=\"Container MACHINE vocabulary (same words as `machine`: x86-64/x86/AArch64/ARM/i386), NOT the toolchain \"\n             \"arch token. Go ELF: use ELF e_machine `x86-64`, NEVER the Go buildinfo GOARCH `amd64`.\",\n        confirmed=tuple(sorted(set(K.ELF_MACHINE.values()) | set(K.PE_MACHINE.values()))),\n        rejected=tuple(K.ARCHITECTURE_REJECTED) + (\"arm64\", \"386\", \"x86_64\"),\n        examples=(\"Go ELF GOARCH=amd64 -> x86-64\", \"Go PE .exe Machine 0x8664 -> x86-64 (D4/D5/D7 Mastery set2)\"),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"names\",),\n        rule=\"ELF section_names = pyelftools [s.name for s in iter_sections()] INCLUDING the leading \\\"\\\" NULL section \"\n             \"(dropping it is rejected). Preserve table order.\",\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"symbols\",),\n        rule=\"ELF symbols = [s.name for s in .symtab] in table order, dupes kept; drop only the empty \\\"\\\" names. \"\n             \".NET assemblies use metadata, not .symtab.\",\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"version\",),\n        rule=\".NET metadata_version = the CLI metadata root (BSJB) version string, e.g. `v4.0.30319` — NOT net8.0 / the \"\n             \"target-framework moniker / the assembly version.\",\n        examples=(\"BSJB root -> v4.0.30319\",),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(BINARY,), families=(\"offset\",),\n        rule=\"`hcfg_offset` = plain decimal FILE offset (not VA) of the stored config's first byte: base64-stored blob -> \"\n             \"the first base64 char (after any length/cap header); RAW blob -> the 'H' of the b'HCFG' magic. Never \"\n             \"'none' when a config was decoded.\",\n        examples=(\"Nim b64 text at 0x77e8 -> 30696 (D9)\", \"D b64 text -> 368272 (D11)\", \"FPC raw HCFG at 0x143f0 -> 82928 (D12)\",\n                  \"Crystal String literal: b64 text at 0x88c3c (header 12 B earlier) -> 560188 (D13)\"),\n    ),\n    # ---- metadata-forensics ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(METADATA,), families=(\"guid\",),\n        rule=\"A GUID's spelling follows its SOURCE, not answer_format. `dotnet-mvid-guid` = Module table Mvid -> #GUID \"\n             \"heap (1-based, 16 B) as .NET Guid.ToString(): first three groups little-endian, lowercase 8-4-4-4-12, no \"\n             \"braces (uuid.UUID(bytes_le=...)). `msi-product-code-guid` = MSI Property table ProductCode string \"\n             \"VERBATIM: uppercase WITH braces (not UpgradeCode / ComponentId / SummaryInfo PackageCode).\",\n        rejected=tuple(K.MSI_PRODUCT_CODE_GUID_REJECTED),\n        examples=(\"#GUID f3 10 e4 21 77 c9 5c 46 .. -> 21e410f3-c977-465c-.. (D12)\",\n                  \"Property ProductCode -> {DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61} (D13; bare form rejected)\"),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(METADATA,), families=(\"hex\",),\n        rule=\"Header integer `<fmt>.<field>_hex` = `0x` + LOWERCASE hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width (u16 -> 4, \"\n             \"u32 -> 8, u64 -> 16 digits), even when the id names no width and answer_format only says 'lowercase \"\n             \"hexadecimal with a 0x prefix'; on PE32+ too (the width is the field's, not the PE flavour). Read the raw \"\n             \"field (an `_rva` is the RVA, not ImageBase+RVA). Byte-prefix fields (`magic_prefix_hex_N`) have NO `0x`.\",\n        rejected=tuple(K.PE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_REJECTED),\n        examples=(\"COFF Machine u16 0x14c -> 0x014c (D9)\", \"AddressOfEntryPoint u32 0x65bd0 -> 0x00065bd0 (D10)\"),\n        derive=_hex_width_derive,\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(METADATA,), families=(\"filename\",),\n        rule=\"A `..-filename` id is the member's OWN name (basename after '->') ONLY when no `version` token precedes it; \"\n             \"`<fmt>.version_<field>` (`d09-pe-NNN-pe-version-original-filename`) = the PE VS_VERSIONINFO StringFileInfo \"\n             \"string verbatim (OriginalFilename), never the randomized member name. The id holds `-pe-` twice: take the \"\n             \"field after the LAST one.\",\n        examples=(\"telemetry-agent-001.exe OriginalFilename -> pe-base-386.exe (D11)\",),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(METADATA,), families=(\"windows\", \"path\"),\n        rule=\"`lnk.target_path_windows` = the shortcut's LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+ CommonPathSuffix; Unicode offsets \"\n             \"when LinkInfoHeaderSize >= 0x24) VERBATIM with backslashes, else the LinkTargetIDList path (drive item + \"\n             \"file-entry long names). Never the WorkingDir / RelativePath / the .lnk member name.\",\n        examples=(\"shortcut-001.lnk LinkInfo -> C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\cmd.exe (D14; IDList agreed)\",),\n# the 'H' of the magic (\"82928\" = 0x143f0, all sets). The solver's raw-scan path retu